# Companion Atlas — LOCAL DEV env. Copy to .env.dev.
#
# ── MODE A: MOCK (default) — zero external services ────────────────────────
# Leave COMPANION_OIDC_ISSUER and CI_MEMORY_URL empty. The API runs every
# request as ATLAS_DEV_SUBJECT with `*` scope; memory queries return nothing.
COMPANION_OIDC_ISSUER=
CI_MEMORY_URL=
ATLAS_DEV_SUBJECT=dev-operator

# ── MODE B: CONNECTED — point at a running CI-Portal + CI-Server ────────────
# Uncomment and adjust. CI-Portal (better-auth) issuer is `<origin>/api/auth`.
# Local Portal dev origin is https://hub.ci.localhost; tailnet/cloud vary.
#
#   COMPANION_OIDC_ISSUER=https://hub.ci.localhost/api/auth
#   COMPANION_OIDC_AUDIENCE=companion-atlas
#   # CI-Server GraphQL — direct dev process is :3030/graphql; via proxy /api/graphql.
#   CI_MEMORY_URL=http://localhost:3030/graphql
#   # A service token if not fronted by the Hub (which injects CI_MEMORY_TOKEN):
#   CI_MEMORY_TOKEN=
#   # Or a scoped CI-Server API key:
#   CI_MEMORY_API_KEY=
#
# NOTE (Portal): `companion-atlas` must be added to PUBLIC_CLIENTS in CI-Portal
# (a Portal PR — see docs/INTEGRATION.md). Local/`.ts.net`/`.local` redirect URIs
# are auto-allowed, so no Portal record is needed for local dev.
# NOTE (CI-Server): the Portal-token path needs PORTAL_OIDC_ENABLED=true and
# `companion-atlas` in the server's PORTAL_OIDC_AUDIENCE allowlist (or mint the
# token with aud=ci-server). Otherwise use a CI-Server JWT / API key.

# ── Viewer (viewer-react) — SPA login (Authorization Code + PKCE) ──────────
# VITE_OIDC_ISSUER=https://hub.ci.localhost/api/auth
# VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=companion-atlas
# VITE_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:4174/auth/callback
# VITE_ATLAS_API=http://localhost:8787/api
# VITE_CESIUM_ION_TOKEN=            # optional; omit for offline/local imagery
